1
00:00:00,250 --> 00:00:02,970
A little party for our team.

2
00:00:03,120 --> 00:00:07,600
Decorations, cake, six happy people. I have a
perfect plan.

3
00:00:07,750 --> 00:00:09,590
Leave room for surprises.

4
00:00:09,740 --> 00:00:13,780
Could the surprises come after dessert this
time, please?

5
00:00:15,250 --> 00:00:17,984
Six plates. One for each of us.

6
00:00:18,134 --> 00:00:21,629
Aunt Rose is stopping by, but she cannot stay.

7
00:00:21,779 --> 00:00:24,513
Can we still show her the party?

8
00:00:24,663 --> 00:00:29,300
Then the six places are for us. We can still
say hello.

9
00:00:30,250 --> 00:00:33,410
We have one strawberry. Just in case.

10
00:00:33,560 --> 00:00:35,840
A very small emergency cake.

11
00:00:35,990 --> 00:00:39,150
Let us wait for the real one.

12
00:00:39,300 --> 00:00:43,780
Couldn't hurt to keep the little one on
standby, though.

13
00:00:45,250 --> 00:00:48,410
A little ribbon for your family party.

14
00:00:48,560 --> 00:00:52,160
Thank you, Rose. Can you stay a moment?

15
00:00:52,310 --> 00:00:54,150
Just a moment, sister.

16
00:00:54,300 --> 00:00:59,220
Good. You can see what the ribbon's for before
you go.

17
00:01:00,250 --> 00:01:02,530
Mine keeps becoming a knot.

18
00:01:02,680 --> 00:01:05,400
Give the loops a little room.

19
00:01:05,550 --> 00:01:07,390
People need that too.

20
00:01:07,540 --> 00:01:12,460
There. It looks more like a bow when I loosen
it.

21
00:01:15,250 --> 00:01:17,743
Today I have checked absolutely everything.

22
00:01:17,893 --> 00:01:21,998
Then you will know where to start if something
changes.

23
00:01:22,148 --> 00:01:24,641
That sounds like a useful plan.

24
00:01:24,791 --> 00:01:29,300
I think I'll keep the checklist where I can
find it.

25
00:01:30,250 --> 00:01:34,290
We will save you a story about the party.

26
00:01:34,440 --> 00:01:37,160
That travels better than cake. Goodbye!

27
00:01:37,310 --> 00:01:39,150
See you soon, Rose.

28
00:01:39,300 --> 00:01:43,340
I'll remember the funny parts to tell you
later.

29
00:01:45,250 --> 00:01:47,900
A bow at the right address.

30
00:01:48,050 --> 00:01:51,128
That is an excellent place for it.

31
00:01:51,278 --> 00:01:54,786
And the bell can still do its job.

32
00:01:54,936 --> 00:01:59,300
Good. We want to hear it when the cake comes.

33
00:02:00,250 --> 00:02:02,805
The entrance is still clear.

34
00:02:02,955 --> 00:02:05,510
The party can get in.

35
00:02:05,660 --> 00:02:07,722
So can the people.

36
00:02:07,872 --> 00:02:12,400
Good. No one has to step over our decorations.

37
00:02:15,250 --> 00:02:17,530
No ribbon under anyone’s feet.

38
00:02:17,680 --> 00:02:20,400
No mystery leftovers on the counter.

39
00:02:20,550 --> 00:02:23,270
Now we can enjoy the room.

40
00:02:23,420 --> 00:02:27,460
I can still see the bow from the doorway.

41
00:02:30,250 --> 00:02:32,970
Our address is fourteen Maple Lane.

42
00:02:33,120 --> 00:02:34,960
Blue door, number fourteen.

43
00:02:35,110 --> 00:02:39,150
Even I cannot confuse the door with the cake.

44
00:02:39,300 --> 00:02:43,780
I'd like to see the cake try wearing our bow.

45
00:02:45,250 --> 00:02:47,970
Fourteen Maple Lane. Delivery around two.

46
00:02:48,120 --> 00:02:49,960
Correct address, correct cake.

47
00:02:50,110 --> 00:02:54,590
The confirmation is correct. We will check the
delivery too.

48
00:02:54,740 --> 00:02:59,220
Fair. An order number can't ring our bell by
itself.

49
00:03:00,250 --> 00:03:02,530
A space for the box.

50
00:03:02,680 --> 00:03:06,280
The strawberry has a very large neighbor
coming.

51
00:03:06,430 --> 00:03:08,710
They will both stay cool.

52
00:03:08,860 --> 00:03:13,340
Good. Let's keep that space open till the
doorbell rings.

53
00:03:15,250 --> 00:03:19,356
I will not check the cake until I see it.

54
00:03:19,506 --> 00:03:22,805
There is room for that on the list.

55
00:03:22,955 --> 00:03:25,044
And room in the fridge.

56
00:03:25,194 --> 00:03:29,300
Then the checkmark waits until the box is
actually here.

57
00:03:30,250 --> 00:03:32,970
Dear cake, welcome to our table.

58
00:03:33,120 --> 00:03:35,400
It may need directions first.

59
00:03:35,550 --> 00:03:38,710
We will welcome it when it arrives.

60
00:03:38,860 --> 00:03:43,780
Okay. I'll save my welcome speech until it can
hear me.

61
00:03:45,250 --> 00:03:47,229
A very punctual napkin.

62
00:03:47,379 --> 00:03:49,831
There is a delivery message.

63
00:03:49,981 --> 00:03:52,906
Let us see what it says.

64
00:03:53,056 --> 00:03:57,400
A message before a doorbell? That's worth a
look.

65
00:04:00,250 --> 00:04:02,530
It says delivered at two-oh-six.

66
00:04:02,680 --> 00:04:05,840
Then why is the cake not here?

67
00:04:05,990 --> 00:04:08,710
Let us check before we guess.

68
00:04:08,860 --> 00:04:13,780
The time tells us when. We still need to know
where.

69
00:04:15,250 --> 00:04:17,530
No box on the step.

70
00:04:17,680 --> 00:04:20,400
Not even a very small one.

71
00:04:20,550 --> 00:04:23,270
Good. That is one place checked.

72
00:04:23,420 --> 00:04:28,340
Well, at least we're sure it isn't behind our
own door.

73
00:04:30,250 --> 00:04:32,403
No cake in the fridge.

74
00:04:32,553 --> 00:04:34,707
No cake beside the board.

75
00:04:34,857 --> 00:04:39,503
Then we are looking for a delivery, not a
hidden dessert.

76
00:04:39,653 --> 00:04:44,300
Good. The whole box wouldn't fit inside that
little dish anyway.

77
00:04:45,250 --> 00:04:48,329
I wanted one afternoon without a mix-up.

78
00:04:48,479 --> 00:04:51,557
We can still have a good afternoon.

79
00:04:51,707 --> 00:04:54,786
First, let us find out what happened.

80
00:04:54,936 --> 00:04:59,300
All right. I'll start by listening to what we
know.

81
00:05:00,250 --> 00:05:02,090
The order numbers match.

82
00:05:02,240 --> 00:05:05,400
So the message is about our cake.

83
00:05:05,550 --> 00:05:08,710
A clue. Much better than a complaint.

84
00:05:08,860 --> 00:05:13,340
Good. We know which order to ask the bakery
about.

85
00:05:15,250 --> 00:05:17,403
Did somebody steal our party?

86
00:05:17,553 --> 00:05:22,616
We do not know that. A delivery could go to
another door.

87
00:05:22,766 --> 00:05:24,503
There is a photo.

88
00:05:24,653 --> 00:05:29,300
Let's look. Maybe the step will tell us where
it went.

89
00:05:30,250 --> 00:05:32,152
That door is green.

90
00:05:32,302 --> 00:05:33,749
Ours is blue.

91
00:05:33,899 --> 00:05:37,165
Then the box was photographed somewhere else.

92
00:05:37,315 --> 00:05:42,400
That's the first clue we can see without
reading any numbers.

93
00:05:45,250 --> 00:05:47,970
No bow in the photo either.

94
00:05:48,120 --> 00:05:50,400
Our cake missed the decorations.

95
00:05:50,550 --> 00:05:54,590
The picture can help us ask a clear question.

96
00:05:54,740 --> 00:05:58,780
Good. We can describe what's actually in the
picture.

97
00:06:00,250 --> 00:06:02,090
Should I order another?

98
00:06:02,240 --> 00:06:04,960
First check where this one went.

99
00:06:05,110 --> 00:06:08,270
One missing cake is enough to investigate.

100
00:06:08,420 --> 00:06:13,340
Fair. Six people don't need two cakes turning
up at once.

101
00:06:15,250 --> 00:06:20,043
Our order is marked delivered, but the photo
shows another door.

102
00:06:20,193 --> 00:06:21,557
Clear and polite.

103
00:06:21,707 --> 00:06:24,786
With actual facts. I like this version.

104
00:06:24,936 --> 00:06:29,300
Good. That gives support something they can
check for us.

105
00:06:30,250 --> 00:06:32,403
The emergency strawberry is ready.

106
00:06:32,553 --> 00:06:35,538
It is one strawberry for six people.

107
00:06:35,688 --> 00:06:39,088
Let us give the cake a chance first.

108
00:06:39,238 --> 00:06:44,300
Good. Cutting one berry six ways sounds like a
very small party.

109
00:06:45,250 --> 00:06:47,970
There must be several green doors.

110
00:06:48,120 --> 00:06:50,840
We need the right green door.

111
00:06:50,990 --> 00:06:54,590
And we can ask before entering anyone’s space.

112
00:06:54,740 --> 00:06:59,220
Right. A green door is a clue, not an
invitation.

113
00:07:00,250 --> 00:07:01,650
A leaf-shaped knocker.

114
00:07:01,800 --> 00:07:05,400
And that little hedge. I know that hedge.

115
00:07:05,550 --> 00:07:08,270
Let us check the number too.

116
00:07:08,420 --> 00:07:12,460
Good. Lots of leaves look alike from this
distance.

117
00:07:15,250 --> 00:07:17,900
I cannot read that last digit.

118
00:07:18,050 --> 00:07:20,271
Then do not guess it.

119
00:07:20,421 --> 00:07:24,357
We can compare the actual number at the door.

120
00:07:24,507 --> 00:07:29,300
Fair. One blurry digit isn't enough to knock
on someone's door.

121
00:07:30,250 --> 00:07:32,530
The driver recorded number eighteen.

122
00:07:32,680 --> 00:07:34,520
Our confirmation says fourteen.

123
00:07:34,670 --> 00:07:37,830
Now we have two numbers to compare.

124
00:07:37,980 --> 00:07:42,460
Good. Eighteen is something we can actually go
and check.

125
00:07:45,250 --> 00:07:50,170
We can ask, did a cake for number fourteen
arrive here?

126
00:07:50,320 --> 00:07:53,480
Better than, where is our entire party?

127
00:07:53,630 --> 00:07:54,590
Much better.

128
00:07:54,740 --> 00:07:59,220
And it sounds friendlier if you're on the
other side.

129
00:08:00,250 --> 00:08:02,530
We will all go together.

130
00:08:02,680 --> 00:08:05,840
Just along this sidewalk. No road crossing.

131
00:08:05,990 --> 00:08:08,710
And straight back if nobody answers.

132
00:08:08,860 --> 00:08:12,900
Good. I'll keep my eyes on the house numbers.

133
00:08:15,250 --> 00:08:18,410
Blue door behind us, green door ahead.

134
00:08:18,560 --> 00:08:21,280
We are checking the actual signs.

135
00:08:21,430 --> 00:08:24,150
The sidewalk is doing excellent work.

136
00:08:24,300 --> 00:08:28,340
It can't read the numbers for us, though, Dad.

137
00:08:30,250 --> 00:08:32,090
The same low hedge.

138
00:08:32,240 --> 00:08:35,400
I recognized it without asking a statue.

139
00:08:35,550 --> 00:08:38,270
A useful improvement over the park.

140
00:08:38,420 --> 00:08:42,900
I much prefer hedges. They don't pretend to
know directions.

141
00:08:45,250 --> 00:08:46,210
Number eighteen.

142
00:08:46,360 --> 00:08:48,200
Different number, different door.

143
00:08:48,350 --> 00:08:51,070
The delivery photo matches this place.

144
00:08:51,220 --> 00:08:55,260
We should still ask whose box it really is.

145
00:08:55,410 --> 00:08:58,570
Right. We'll let the neighbor tell us.

146
00:09:00,250 --> 00:09:03,175
Can we peek through the hedge?

147
00:09:03,325 --> 00:09:06,250
We can ring the bell instead.

148
00:09:06,400 --> 00:09:07,906
Much less scratchy.

149
00:09:08,056 --> 00:09:12,400
Good. I'll keep my nose out of that hedge.

150
00:09:15,250 --> 00:09:18,410
This is the door in the photograph.

151
00:09:18,560 --> 00:09:20,400
One question, calmly asked.

152
00:09:20,550 --> 00:09:22,390
We are all here.

153
00:09:22,540 --> 00:09:27,900
And the box in that photo hasn't told us whose
it is.

154
00:09:30,250 --> 00:09:31,650
Now we wait.

155
00:09:31,800 --> 00:09:33,640
I can do that.

156
00:09:33,790 --> 00:09:36,070
You have had pancake practice.

157
00:09:36,220 --> 00:09:40,260
Good. Apparently that pan was preparing me for
doorbells.

158
00:09:40,410 --> 00:09:43,570
At least the doorbell doesn't need flipping.

159
00:09:45,250 --> 00:09:47,970
Maybe the cake answered the door.

160
00:09:48,120 --> 00:09:50,840
Cakes are very poor at doorbells.

161
00:09:50,990 --> 00:09:54,150
Let us give our neighbor a moment.

162
00:09:54,300 --> 00:09:59,220
Fine. I'll keep the welcome speech till we
have an answer.

163
00:10:00,250 --> 00:10:04,237
If nobody is home, we will ask the bakery
again.

164
00:10:04,387 --> 00:10:07,592
Yes. We do not need to look around.

165
00:10:07,742 --> 00:10:10,163
We have already found useful clues.

166
00:10:10,313 --> 00:10:14,300
Right. We can tell them where the photo was
taken.

167
00:10:15,250 --> 00:10:16,650
Someone is coming.

168
00:10:16,800 --> 00:10:17,760
Good afternoon.

169
00:10:17,910 --> 00:10:19,750
Thank you for answering.

170
00:10:19,900 --> 00:10:24,380
We only need a moment to ask about the
delivery.

171
00:10:24,530 --> 00:10:27,690
We have our order number right here.

172
00:10:30,250 --> 00:10:32,970
Hello. We are from number fourteen.

173
00:10:33,120 --> 00:10:38,480
We are checking a delivery that may have
reached the wrong door.

174
00:10:38,630 --> 00:10:40,030
A cake delivery.

175
00:10:40,180 --> 00:10:44,220
The photo looks like the step outside your
door.

176
00:10:45,250 --> 00:10:48,850
A white bakery box with a red seal.

177
00:10:49,000 --> 00:10:52,160
The photo shows it beside this door.

178
00:10:52,310 --> 00:10:54,590
We have the order confirmation.

179
00:10:54,740 --> 00:10:58,780
We can show the matching number if that helps.

180
00:11:00,250 --> 00:11:03,850
Did a cake for number fourteen arrive here?

181
00:11:04,000 --> 00:11:08,040
We think there may have been a number mix-up.

182
00:11:08,190 --> 00:11:09,150
No hurry.

183
00:11:09,300 --> 00:11:13,780
We brought our confirmation if you'd like to
compare it.

184
00:11:15,250 --> 00:11:17,530
That sounds like a fridge.

185
00:11:17,680 --> 00:11:20,840
Let us hear what our neighbor says.

186
00:11:20,990 --> 00:11:23,710
Yes. We still need to check.

187
00:11:23,860 --> 00:11:27,900
Good. A fridge sound can't tell us what's
inside.

188
00:11:30,250 --> 00:11:32,970
Same order number, same white box.

189
00:11:33,120 --> 00:11:35,400
That will help identify it.

190
00:11:35,550 --> 00:11:37,830
And explain the mistake clearly.

191
00:11:37,980 --> 00:11:42,900
That'll tell us more than just the color of
the door.

192
00:11:45,250 --> 00:11:48,850
Thank you for helping us sort this out.

193
00:11:49,000 --> 00:11:51,720
Our plates are waiting very patiently.

194
00:11:51,870 --> 00:11:53,270
So are we.

195
00:11:53,420 --> 00:11:57,900
My plate's got a bit more patience than my
stomach.

196
00:12:00,250 --> 00:12:03,846
My perfect plan did not include asking for
help.

197
00:12:03,996 --> 00:12:06,808
There is still time to add that.

198
00:12:06,958 --> 00:12:10,163
It is a useful line on any list.

199
00:12:10,313 --> 00:12:14,300
I'm adding that one to the plan in my head.

200
00:12:15,250 --> 00:12:16,650
A white box.

201
00:12:16,800 --> 00:12:18,640
With a red seal.

202
00:12:18,790 --> 00:12:22,830
Let us check it before we carry it home.

203
00:12:22,980 --> 00:12:27,460
Good. A white box alone could hold somebody
else's dessert.

204
00:12:30,250 --> 00:12:32,607
That is our order number.

205
00:12:32,757 --> 00:12:34,658
And our cake description.

206
00:12:34,808 --> 00:12:38,074
Now we can ask about the label.

207
00:12:38,224 --> 00:12:42,400
Good. The handwriting and our address still
need comparing.

208
00:12:45,250 --> 00:12:47,530
The order ends in ten-C.

209
00:12:47,680 --> 00:12:49,520
So does the sticker.

210
00:12:49,670 --> 00:12:55,030
The plain round cake. We have checked more
than the box color.

211
00:12:55,180 --> 00:12:59,220
Good. Now let's hear what happened when it
arrived.

212
00:13:00,250 --> 00:13:05,170
This came to eighteen. I put it straight in
the fridge.

213
00:13:05,320 --> 00:13:08,040
Thank you for keeping it cool.

214
00:13:08,190 --> 00:13:09,590
We appreciate that.

215
00:13:09,740 --> 00:13:14,220
I'm glad you heard the delivery. Our bell
never rang.

216
00:13:15,250 --> 00:13:18,454
The label looked like eighteen to the driver.

217
00:13:18,604 --> 00:13:20,242
Our confirmation says fourteen.

218
00:13:20,392 --> 00:13:24,379
A small mark sent a large cake on a visit.

219
00:13:24,529 --> 00:13:29,300
Good. We can give the bakery the number that
caused the mix-up.

220
00:13:30,250 --> 00:13:32,530
I have not opened it.

221
00:13:32,680 --> 00:13:34,520
The seal is intact.

222
00:13:34,670 --> 00:13:38,270
Thank you. We will take it straight home.

223
00:13:38,420 --> 00:13:43,780
Good. That red seal looks just like the one in
the photo.

224
00:13:45,250 --> 00:13:47,900
Here you are. Enjoy your party.

225
00:13:48,050 --> 00:13:51,557
Thank you for being a very good neighbor.

226
00:13:51,707 --> 00:13:54,786
Our cake has had quite a trip.

227
00:13:54,936 --> 00:13:59,300
And a very kind person looked after it. Thank
you.

228
00:14:00,250 --> 00:14:01,614
Thank you again.

229
00:14:01,764 --> 00:14:05,700
We will tell the bakery it is safely
recovered.

230
00:14:05,850 --> 00:14:09,357
And we will check every digit next time.

231
00:14:09,507 --> 00:14:14,300
Good. I want the bakery to know which address
caused it.

232
00:14:15,250 --> 00:14:17,970
Does it need a ticket home?

233
00:14:18,120 --> 00:14:20,840
Just a steady pair of hands.

234
00:14:20,990 --> 00:14:23,710
I have checked both of mine.

235
00:14:23,860 --> 00:14:27,900
Good. My job can be keeping the sidewalk
clear.

236
00:14:30,250 --> 00:14:32,152
Blue door, number fourteen.

237
00:14:32,302 --> 00:14:34,658
At last, the correct entrance.

238
00:14:34,808 --> 00:14:37,165
Straight to the fridge first.

239
00:14:37,315 --> 00:14:42,400
Understood. This stop is only for dropping off
our cold passenger.

240
00:14:45,250 --> 00:14:48,410
A safe place while we get ready.

241
00:14:48,560 --> 00:14:51,720
The party can wait two more minutes.

242
00:14:51,870 --> 00:14:54,590
We have found something worth celebrating.

243
00:14:54,740 --> 00:14:59,220
And the little strawberry's got its neighbor
back at last.

244
00:15:00,250 --> 00:15:04,186
Recovered safely from number eighteen. Please
check the label.

245
00:15:04,336 --> 00:15:06,557
Fourteen is still our address.

246
00:15:06,707 --> 00:15:09,357
And thank you for the help.

247
00:15:09,507 --> 00:15:14,300
Good. They'll know they can close the search
for our cake.

248
00:15:15,250 --> 00:15:17,530
Clean hands before we serve.

249
00:15:17,680 --> 00:15:20,840
The cake traveled farther than we did.

250
00:15:20,990 --> 00:15:23,270
Its box did the traveling.

251
00:15:23,420 --> 00:15:28,340
And everybody who handled that box can wash up
for dessert.

252
00:15:30,250 --> 00:15:33,952
May I have the emergency strawberry with my
slice?

253
00:15:34,102 --> 00:15:36,998
Yes. It can retire from emergency duty.

254
00:15:37,148 --> 00:15:39,641
One berry, one very important job.

255
00:15:39,791 --> 00:15:44,300
I think it deserves a very good seat on my
plate.

256
00:15:45,250 --> 00:15:47,970
Here is our guest of honor.

257
00:15:48,120 --> 00:15:49,960
Same order, right house.

258
00:15:50,110 --> 00:15:53,710
And still cool. We can serve it now.

259
00:15:53,860 --> 00:15:58,340
I'll save my welcome till we actually have our
slices.

260
00:16:00,250 --> 00:16:02,530
The box is finally empty.

261
00:16:02,680 --> 00:16:06,280
The cake has a much better view now.

262
00:16:06,430 --> 00:16:08,710
And space for six servings.

263
00:16:08,860 --> 00:16:12,900
Good. Every plate has a person waiting for it.

264
00:16:15,250 --> 00:16:16,819
Six equal slices.

265
00:16:16,969 --> 00:16:19,031
No four-or-forty problem today.

266
00:16:19,181 --> 00:16:22,229
Just six people sharing one cake.

267
00:16:22,379 --> 00:16:27,400
I like this math. Everybody gets the very same
share.

268
00:16:30,250 --> 00:16:32,970
One for Dan, one for Leo.

269
00:16:33,120 --> 00:16:34,960
A very successful delivery.

270
00:16:35,110 --> 00:16:37,830
This time we saw it arrive.

271
00:16:37,980 --> 00:16:42,900
Good. I can confirm this slice is at the right
address.

272
00:16:45,250 --> 00:16:47,530
Two left on the board.

273
00:16:47,680 --> 00:16:50,400
One for Nina, one for Max.

274
00:16:50,550 --> 00:16:53,270
Exactly. No one has to guess.

275
00:16:53,420 --> 00:16:57,460
Good. I can count them from my own place.

276
00:17:00,250 --> 00:17:02,607
My slice has an assistant.

277
00:17:02,757 --> 00:17:04,204
The emergency strawberry.

278
00:17:04,354 --> 00:17:06,710
Six slices. Everyone has one.

279
00:17:06,860 --> 00:17:12,400
Good. It was a long trip for this little bit
of cake.

280
00:17:15,250 --> 00:17:19,897
The cake is with the family. The sharp tools
stay here.

281
00:17:20,047 --> 00:17:22,616
That is a good final check.

282
00:17:22,766 --> 00:17:25,750
Can I call the job done now?

283
00:17:25,900 --> 00:17:29,300
Yes. Come sit down and enjoy your slice.

284
00:17:30,250 --> 00:17:32,530
I wanted a perfect party.

285
00:17:32,680 --> 00:17:35,840
You made room for a real one.

286
00:17:35,990 --> 00:17:38,270
We found the cake together.

287
00:17:38,420 --> 00:17:43,340
That's the part I want to remember when we
tell it.

288
00:17:45,250 --> 00:17:47,607
To this very helpful team.

289
00:17:47,757 --> 00:17:49,658
And our kind neighbor.

290
00:17:49,808 --> 00:17:52,165
And checking the whole address.

291
00:17:52,315 --> 00:17:57,400
And the person who noticed the green door in
the picture.

292
00:18:00,250 --> 00:18:02,900
Did the family party start yet?

293
00:18:03,050 --> 00:18:06,557
Almost, Dad. Our cake visited the neighbor
first.

294
00:18:06,707 --> 00:18:09,357
It came back with a story.

295
00:18:09,507 --> 00:18:14,300
We'll tell you the whole thing once we taste
it, Ed.

296
00:18:15,250 --> 00:18:19,290
A clear address is better than a lucky guess.

297
00:18:19,440 --> 00:18:22,600
We have been collecting evidence for that.

298
00:18:22,750 --> 00:18:24,590
Thanks, Dad. Talk soon.

299
00:18:24,740 --> 00:18:29,220
Bye, Grandpa. We even read the little print
this time.

300
00:18:30,250 --> 00:18:31,650
Sweet. Not sour.

301
00:18:31,800 --> 00:18:34,080
And no flowers in it.

302
00:18:34,230 --> 00:18:36,510
Just a very welcome cake.

303
00:18:36,660 --> 00:18:40,700
This one definitely got the right kind of
flour.

304
00:18:40,850 --> 00:18:44,010
And I'm glad it found this table.

305
00:18:45,250 --> 00:18:48,410
The ribbons were not the best part.

306
00:18:48,560 --> 00:18:49,520
What was?

307
00:18:49,670 --> 00:18:53,270
Everyone staying with the problem. And with
me.

308
00:18:53,420 --> 00:18:58,780
I'd stay with you even if the strawberry were
all we had.

309
00:19:00,250 --> 00:19:03,516
You do not have to guess alone.

310
00:19:03,666 --> 00:19:06,477
Even when your checklist looks impressive.

311
00:19:06,627 --> 00:19:07,620
Especially then.

312
00:19:07,770 --> 00:19:12,400
A second pair of eyes doesn't take up much
room.

313
00:19:15,250 --> 00:19:18,516
Emergency strawberry, thank you for your
service.

314
00:19:18,666 --> 00:19:20,568
A very small hero.

315
00:19:20,718 --> 00:19:22,165
With excellent timing.

316
00:19:22,315 --> 00:19:27,400
Good. Nobody else had to share one tiny berry
six ways.

317
00:19:30,250 --> 00:19:34,926
Would anyone like to stay right here for a
while?

318
00:19:35,076 --> 00:19:35,963
Yes.

319
00:19:36,113 --> 00:19:37,574
No directions required.

320
00:19:37,724 --> 00:19:42,400
Fine by me. I know exactly where my plate is.

321
00:19:45,250 --> 00:19:47,970
The party found the right house.

322
00:19:48,120 --> 00:19:51,280
It had the right people all along.

323
00:19:51,430 --> 00:19:55,470
Everybody has a slice. Who's going to tell
Rose?

324
00:19:55,620 --> 00:19:58,780
Me. I'll start with the little strawberry.
